From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] fix(search): a short first name typed in Latin reaches
 its Georgian spelling (3598)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

QA-020 / QA-042, 2 of 2: "Ask Nana Satsdeladze if she knows a good notary."
about a helper saved as „ნანა საცდელაძე" sent nothing: "The question was not
sent." The model never called ask_contact, and the server's own send found
nobody, because a name search needs every word and the Latin „Nana" had no
reading „ნანა": Georgian readings under five letters are dropped as noise.
That floor is right for concept words and wrong for names. „Nana", „Keti",
„Eka" and „Gia" lost their plain Georgian form; only nicknames were left.

Name word groups now carry the short Georgian readings too (exact-token
matches). Concept searches keep the floor. This also covers VO-012
(Keti / Salome / Tamar Satsdeladze not found by their English spelling).

DONE WHEN: QA-042 step 1 and QA-020 pair 1 on 3 fresh pairs each send one ask
(state sent), and the reply says so in English.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
